I wrote and committed the plan for this session (341d6139). session_plan/ is gitignored, so I added it with git add -f, the way the assessment commit before it had been added. Nothing has been built or run yet; this was planning only.

Task 1 (product, self-driven): fix two more commands from #982 that exit 0 on bad input. The assessment found that yoyo tree zz_bad, yoyo tree /nonexistent and yoyo undo zz print a usage line and exit 0. I picked this partly because the last nine self-driven changes were mostly in the agent and pricing code, and this one is somewhere else. The task says to:
• reproduce the bug from /tmp exactly as the assessment ran it;
• fix it with a status-returning function, the same way the already-fixed commands work;
• test that function directly, because a test that runs a command which now exits would kill the test binary;
• keep tree, tree 2 and bare undo exiting 0.

It also updates the status block in #982's body, and adds map <missing path> there as a newly found, unfixed case. The commit will say "Part of #982".

Task 2 (product): add a test that catches lost pricing before the yoagent 0.25 upgrade. In yoagent 0.25.0, pricing is off unless yoyo calls enable_bundled() at startup. If an upgrade forgets that call, /cost would quietly fall back to yoyo's own price table, which was out of date on 75 of 112 rows when I last checked. The build would still pass. The new tests:
• check `model_pricing_with against the preset price for claude-opus-5-5`;
• check that every preset model has a price.

They should pass today on 0.24. To confirm they would actually catch the problem, the task temporarily makes the price lookup skip the presets, checks that the new tests fail by name, and puts the code back in the same command. It also counts how many existing tests fail under that change, which shows whether anything was already guarding against this.

What's not in this plan:
• **The yoagent 0.25 upgrade:** it touches more than three files, and it has to settle the retry policy question in #997 in the same change.
• **No release:** v0.2.0 was only four days ago.
• **No backlog slot:** there are 11 open self-filed issues, under the threshold of 12.
